Build Letter Hunt 002 as a curses-only program on GNU/Linux.

The upstream linuxport Makefile builds the SDL port: it compiles gfx_sdl.cpp,
queries sdl-config, and links SDL.  As BUILD.TXT describes, the curses port
is selected with -DUSE_CURSES and linked with ncurses only; the SDL port and
its alphabet*.bmp fonts are not built.  enummaker and premake no longer
assume enummaker is on PATH, and both Makefiles honour CXX and CXXFLAGS.

Read text.txt, rooms/piecelist.map, and wordlist/wordlist.txt from
LETTERHUNT_DATADIR (".." by default, as upstream) so that the read-only data
can live in the store while letterhunt.sav and hiscore.txt are still written
relative to the working directory.

Include <unistd.h> and <string.h> for usleep, sleep, unlink, memcpy,
memmove, strcpy, strncpy, strcmp, and strdup, which current glibc and GCC no
longer declare implicitly.

diff -r a/src/gfx_curses.cpp b/src/gfx_curses.cpp
--- a/src/gfx_curses.cpp
+++ b/src/gfx_curses.cpp
@@ -51,12 +51,15 @@
 using namespace std;
 
 #include <assert.h>
+#include <string.h>
 
 // Windows specific code
 #ifdef WIN32
 #include <windows.h>
 #define usleep(x) Sleep((x)/1000)
 #define sleep(x) Sleep((x))
+#else
+#include <unistd.h>
 #endif
 
 #include <curses.h>
